{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-torsion-leaf","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:q-torsion-leaf","kind":"example","title":"$q$-Torsion leaf","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-flow"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-connection","tags":["torsion-leaf","archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QTorsionLeaf","text":"q-torsion-leaf.md","leanSource":"q-torsion-leaf.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"ex:q-torsion-leaf\"></a>\n<strong>Example.</strong> <em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Torsion leaf</em></p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H = \\ker\\varTheta \\subset TM</code> be the horizontal distribution on the CR manifold <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M</code>. A <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-torsion leaf is a maximal integral submanifold <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L \\hookrightarrow M</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H</code> invariant under the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed Reeb flow:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  T_p L \\subset H_p \\quad\\text{and}\\quad \\phi_t^q(L) = L.</code></pre>\n"}
